xnu 0126: dump the SE state around a command

The engine accepts the TX/RX command and never starts it for any clock level.
Before guessing further, read the state that decides it: GENI_IF_DISABLE_RO
(0x64, if the FIFO interface is disabled only the DMA path works),
M_CMD_CTRL, SE_IRQ_EN, GENI_OUTPUT_CTRL, the serial clock config and
CLK_CTRL_RO at setup, and after writing the command print GENI_STATUS (is
M_GENI_CMD_ACTIVE set?) and M_CMD0 (did the command stick?).

